d growth. Strategic planning visibility deteriorates with extended examination timeline.","iso":"2026-09-07","paper_title":"Finance, Performance and Risk Monitoring Report Quarter 1 2026-2027","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64123/Executive Finance Performance Risk Monitoring Q1 Report.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Emergency Planning risk (C07) worsened during Q1 2026/27, increasing from Low (6) to Moderate (9)","lead":"Deteriorating operational resilience (Emergency Planning risk increase) and new high-risk on planning governance (C05A) signal emerging vulnerabilities in council's operational and strategic capacity.","iso":"2026-09-07","paper_title":"Finance, Performance and Risk Monitoring Report Quarter 1 2026-2027","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64123/Executive Finance Performance Risk Monitoring Q1 Report.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Finance, Performance and Risk Monitoring Report Quarter 1 2026-2027","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64123/Executive Finance Performance Risk Monitoring Q1 Report.pdf","headline":"Treasury position benefiting from higher interest rates than forecast\u2014\u00a30.249m favourable variance in Executive Matters","detail":"Council's actual year-end underspend of \u00a30.275m includes \u00a30.249m benefit from interest rates running higher than budget forecast. Without this treasury windfall, underlying position would be \u00a30.026m underspend. Benefit is temporary and interest-rate dependent.","category":"income","matters":"Positive in near term but indicates budget assumptions were conservative on rates. Treasury benefit is temporary and masks underlying \u00a30.449m savings non-delivery problem. Council dependent on favourable conditions to balance.","figures":"\u00a30.249m treasury benefit; \u00a30.275m reported underspend would reduce to \u00a30.026m excluding treasury","quote":"Higher Interest rates than forecast -0.249","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Finance, Performance and Risk Monitoring Report Quarter 1 2026-2027","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64123/Executive Finance Performance Risk Monitoring Q1 Report.pdf","headline":"Local Plan examination facing delays; Planning Inspectors carrying out additional work beyond pre-election period","detail":"Local Plan submitted July 2025, examination heard February 2026, but Inspectors' decision letter delayed. On 20 May 2026, Inspectors advised additional technical work required 'beyond that arising from the pre-election period.' New inspector appointed July 2026. Extends planning policy uncertainty.","category":"governance","matters":"Delays in Local Plan adoption extend period of development uncertainty and defer clarity on policy framework for housing and growth. Strategic planning visibility deteriorates with extended examination timeline.","figures":"Examination began February 2026; decision letter delayed; new inspector targeting mid-August 2026","quote":"On 20 May, the Inspectors advised that 'due to the technical nature of the matters discussed during the hearing sessions, the Inspectors were carrying out additional work to ensure that their letter identifies a robust position from which the examination can progress efficiently. This process has unfortunately resulted in some delay beyond that arising from the pre-election period.'","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Finance, Performance and Risk Monitoring Report Quarter 1 2026-2027","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64123/Executive Finance Performance Risk Monitoring Q1 Report.pdf","headline":"Emergency Planning risk (C07) worsened during Q1 2026/27, increasing from Low (6) to Moderate (9)","detail":"One of only two risk score changes during quarter, indicating deterioration. New risk C05A (Planning Applications for Major Development) also added at Very High rating. Both point to emerging governance and operational risks.","category":"governance","matters":"Deteriorating operational resilience (Emergency Planning risk increase) and new high-risk on planning governance (C05A) signal emerging vulnerabilities in council's operational and strategic capacity.","figures":"C07 score increase from 6 to 9; C05A newly added at Very High","quote":"There was one score change within the register during Quarter 1 2026/27, C07 Emergency Planning increased its score from 6 (Low) to 9 (moderate).","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Finance, Performance and Risk Monitoring Report Quarter 1 2026-2027","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64123/Executive Finance Performance Risk Monitoring Q1 Report.pdf","headline":"Capital programme forecast overspend of \u00a30.644m (1.5% of budget), with Place & Regeneration \u00a30.660m over","detail":"Total capital programme spending \u00a342.733m against budget of \u00a342.089m. Place & Regeneration showing 3.4% overspend on their portfolio, driven substantially by Market Square issues. Capital budget discipline concern.","category":"capital","matters":"Capital overspend indicates slippage in project control and budget management discipline across regeneration portfolio. Lender assesses council's ability to execute capital strategy.","figures":"\u00a342.733m forecast vs \u00a342.089m budget (\u00a30.644m overspend); Place & Regen \u00a30.660m overspend","quote":"Table 5 below summarises the forecast spend against the full capital programme (i.e. spend across all years of the capital programme). The full capital programme is presented in detail in Appendix 1. Total 42.089 42.733 0.644","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Finance, Performance and Risk Monitoring Report Quarter 1 2026-2027","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64123/Executive Finance Performance Risk Monitoring Q1 Report.pdf","headline":"Transforming Market Square Bicester (\u00a35.049m) being reprofiled due to forecast overspend, deferring \u00a30.370m from 2026/27","detail":"Flagship regeneration project is reprofiling \u00a31.181m beyond 2026/27 with explicit reason stated as needing to 'consider the best way forward considering forecast overspend.' Indicates cost control problems on material capital scheme. Project is central to council's economic prosperity strategy.","category":"capital","matters":"Overspend and timeline delays on flagship \u00a35m project signals capital project governance and budget discipline concerns. Regeneration outcomes are core to council's growth strategy and to lender confidence in delivery.","figures":"\u00a35.049m project budget; \u00a30.370m reprofiled from 2026/27; \u00a31.181m reprofiled beyond","quote":"Reprofiling due to the project needing to consider the best way forward considering forecast overspend.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-07"},"name":"Cherwell","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-22","since_iso":"2026-08-23","distress":false,"headline":"Treasury position benefiting from higher interest rates than forecast\u2014\u00a30.249m favourable variance in Executive Matters","lead":"Positive in near term but indicates budget assumptions were conservative on rates. Treasury benefit is temporary and masks underlying \u00a30.449m savings non-delivery problem. Council dependent on favourable conditions to balance.","also":["64 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit and Governance Committee on 2026-09-30","n_findings":65,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Finance, Performance and Risk Monitoring Report Quarter 1 2026-2027","top_paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64123/Executive Finance Performance Risk Monitoring Q1 Report.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":132,"news_drafts_total":3}}